  "summaries": {
    "wheat": [
      "The 2026/27 U.S. wheat outlook is for reduced supplies and exports, lower domestic use, and smaller ending stocks compared with 2025/26. U.S. 2026/27 production is projected at 1.561 billion bushels, down 424 million from the prior year, reflecting sharply lower harvested area.",
      "Total U.S. 2026/27 domestic use is lower on reduced feed and residual use reflecting smaller supplies, while food use is unchanged at 960 million bushels. U.S. 2026/27 exports are projected at 775 million bushels.",
      "Global 2026/27 outlook is for lower supplies, marginally lower consumption, reduced trade, and decreased ending stocks. World production projected at 819.1 MMT, down from the 2025/26 record of 843.8 MMT. World ending stocks fall to 275.0 MMT from 279.2 MMT."
    ],
    "corn": [
      "The 2026/27 U.S. corn outlook is for reductions to supply, total use, and ending stocks with a higher expected farm price. U.S. corn production for 2026/27 projected at 15.995 billion bushels, down 1.026 billion from the prior year's record on lower harvested area and yield.",
      "Total U.S. corn use for 2026/27 is forecast to fall 2 percent relative to a year ago. U.S. corn exports forecast to decline 5 percent to 3.2 billion bushels. With supply falling more than use, 2026/27 ending stocks are down 185 million bushels. Stocks-to-use is 12.1 percent.",
      "World corn production for 2026/27 forecast to decline from the prior year's record to 1.295 billion MMT. Global corn ending stocks for 2026/27 down 19.4 MMT to 277.5 MMT \u2014 which, if realized, would be the lowest since 2012/13."
    ],
    "soybeans": [
      "The 2026/27 outlook for U.S. soybeans shows higher supplies, crush, and exports with lower ending stocks from the 2025/26 forecast. Crush projected at 2.750 billion bushels, up 120 million from 2025/26 on favourable crush margins.",
      "U.S. soybean exports projected to rise to 1.630 billion bushels, an increase over 2025/26 when tariff measures curtailed Chinese purchases. U.S. ending stocks for 2026/27 projected at 310 million bushels, down 30 million from revised 2025/26.",
      "Global 2026/27 oilseed outlook shows higher production, crush, and ending stocks. World soybean production projected at 441.5 MMT. Combined global oilseed crush projected to increase by 4 percent."
    ],
    "soymeal": [
      "World soybean meal production for 2026/27 is projected at 300.4 MMT, up from 290.3 MMT in 2025/26, driven by higher crush volumes in all major origins \u2014 United States, Brazil, and Argentina.",
      "Global soybean meal exports for 2026/27 are projected at 88.2 MMT, reflecting strong demand growth in Asia and continued expansion of livestock sectors in key importing regions.",
      "U.S. soybean meal production for 2026/27 projected at 58.99 thousand short tons, with exports at 21.7 thousand short tons, the highest on record, reflecting competitive FOB values."
    ],
    "soyoil": [
      "Total U.S. soybean oil demand for 2026/27 is forecast to increase 7 percent, with higher domestic use partly offset by lower exports. Biofuel use projected at 17.8 billion pounds, up substantially from 14.2 billion in 2025/26.",
      "World soybean oil production for 2026/27 is projected at 74.7 MMT, up from 71.8 MMT in 2025/26. Global ending stocks projected at 6.32 MMT, recovering from the 5.93 MMT trough in 2025/26.",
      "Argentine soybean oil exports remain the dominant trade flow at 6.55 MMT. U.S. soybean oil exports projected to fall sharply to 0.18 MMT in 2026/27 on higher domestic biofuel demand absorbing available supply."
    ]
  },
